lculated body size, otherwise just use the actual row count so no padding happens. Refining the paginate function to handle both cases properly—with headers, I'll calculate body as the available space minus header and footer, then pass a pad flag to writeColumns to add blank rows if needed; without headers, body becomes the full page length and padding is disabled since we're just formatting whatever lines we have.\n\nWriting paginate function... Writing column layout logic... Writing the padding function... I'm verifying the logic works correctly for different column widths—when the width is a multiple of 8 like 24, tabs land exactly at the boundary, and when it's not like 36, we get the right combination of tabs and spaces to reach the column width.\n\nNow I need to make the actual code changes: updating the paginate function to calculate body height for the no-header case and pass the pad flag, modifying writeColumns to accept a pad parameter and use the new padToCol function instead of padOrTrunc, and replacing all instances of padOrTrunc with padToCol. The strings package Builder is already imported, so I'm ready to start making these edits.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1840,"cache_read_input_tokens":56251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1840},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c4cd373-f64f-4f38-af1e-9e4d6f921541","uuid":"c009eb53-9af6-4114-afe8-6fe330e839f8"}
